// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`r2 purpose text (stage B) > snapshots the r2 description and guidance 1`] = `"LSP answers compiler-known questions about exact symbols and locations. findReferences returns matches grouped by file, each with its source line, enclosing declaration, and role (import, export, declaration, or use); scope accepts an existing workspace-relative file or directory, and pages of 100 continue with the nextCursor bound to the same query. prepareCallHierarchy with incomingCalls returns de-duplicated caller declarations with call-site lines (a lone oversized caller reports callSitesOmitted instead of some sites). hover returns the raw contents plus a plain-text type field. goToDefinition and goToImplementation return definition and implementation locations. Anchors (symbol with optional path) and the investigate recipe (definition, type, references, implementations, callers) cover targets whose coordinates are unknown. Use grep for textual occurrences, comments, strings, and config or non-code files, and read for source content at already-known paths. LSP needs a running language server: where none runs, grep and read are the tools. Positions are 0-based in server.positionEncoding and the server field routes to one exact descriptor; an unavailable envelope is valid. The operation field is an explicit enum; do not invent operations, and foreign fields are tool errors. Rename, formatting, and resolved code actions are proposals; applyProposal through SmartEdit is the mutating operation."`;

exports[`r2 purpose text (stage B) > snapshots the r2 description and guidance 2`] = `
"LSP returns compiler-known answers with their evidence inline: source lines, enclosing declarations, roles, and types.
findReferences takes path, position, and optional scope (an existing workspace-relative file or directory) plus limit; results are grouped by file with source line, enclosing declaration, and role, paging 100 at a time with a nextCursor that must repeat the same path, position, and scope.
investigate accepts one task — definition, type, references, implementations, or callers — with symbol plus optional path XOR path plus position; hover answers carry a plain-text type, and caller answers carry call-site lines with possible callSitesOmitted.
For code actions, use the exact returned actionId and sourceSha256 in selection; resolve with the same path, range, optional context, and routing as discovery. Discovery lists without selecting; resolution previews without applying.
Positions are 0-based in server.positionEncoding; route by exact server id, and treat unavailable as a valid refusal (no server). Rename, formatting, and resolved actions are proposals; only explicit applyProposal mutates via SmartEdit."
`;
